00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.120
<v Chris>prunes exactly what was put there.

68
00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.240
<v Christina>Let's stay on sources, because that's usually where

69
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.740
<v Christina>these systems get thin.

70
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.540
<v Chris>Sourcing is one of the five subsystems here, not an

71
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.680
<v Chris>import script somebody wrote once. A channel is a row

72
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.920
<v Chris>saying where data comes from and how to reach it, and

73
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.920
<v Chris>uploaded content is parsed, chunked and embedded on

74
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:29.540
<v Chris>the way in.

75
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.680
<v Christina>I'm still not moving my warehouse into your database.

76
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.680
<v Chris>You don't have to. What Percolate keeps is how to

77
00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.900
<v Chris>reach the service: the connection, the credential, the

78
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.880
<v Chris>schedule. Pulling from it is a workflow you author and

79
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.760
<v Chris>schedule like any other, so the pipeline feeding the

80
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.400
<v Chris>agent and the agent itself are the same machinery.

81
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.980
<v Christina>Which is the part that gets underestimated.

82
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.140
<v Chris>The hard part of an AI product is the dozen

83
00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:57.460
<v Chris>unglamorous steps that have to run every night so the

84
00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.080
<v Chris>clever bit has something to work with.

85
00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.900
<v Christina>Once it's all in there, how do I ask across it? Some

86
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.060
<v Christina>of it is graph-shaped and some of it is just text.

87
00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.700
<v Chris>Through one dialect called P8QL. A question arrives in

